## Protocol (ported from `mcu_frame_decode.py` + `protocol_definitions_recovered.h`)
Framing `A5 | total_len | {sub_len type mod payload}+ | sum&0xFF | 5A`, `F5 01/02/03` stuffing, little-endian structs (`<ff` speed, `<HhBbbI` battery, `<10B` sensor, `<9h` imu, `<9B` version, `<hhhbB`×4 motors, `<8B` heartbeat). RX is an incremental `FrameParser` (resync, checksum, 8 KiB buffer cap).

## Node behavior
- Params `port:=/dev/serial_mower`, `baud:=115200`, plus frames, `heartbeat_period` (0.1), `speed_cmd_rate`, `cmd_vel_timeout`, `speed_timeout`, `odom_rate`, `linear/angular_scale/max`, `use_imu_yaw`, battery scales. Serial: pyserial when present, **built-in termios raw-8N1 fallback** otherwise (the `ros:humble` image may lack `python3-serial`); reconnect loop, zero-speed frame on shutdown.
- `/battery` (BatteryState, `dock_ok`→charging), `/odom` (dead-reckon from measured `SpeedData`, heading from MCU `ImuData` yaw when fresh, else integrate ω; **degrades to the commanded velocity** with an inflated twist covariance), `/imu` placeholder only while module 9 arrives (**otherwise nothing published** — `SensorInfoControl` is the host→MCU direction of module 10 and carries no IMU data; this is documented in the docstring), `/mower_sensor_info` only if `mower_interfaces` imports, with guarded field assignment (`_set_if`, `speed`→`speed_rpm` alias, `TypeError` tolerated).
- `/cmd_vel` `TwistStamped` → scale+clamp map → `SpeedCommand`/`SpeedData` frames streamed at `speed_cmd_rate`, zeros after `cmd_vel_timeout`. Heartbeat at fixed param period (**documented UNKNOWN**), **PID TODO** (`libpid_controller.so`, gains in `config/base.yaml`), **estop passthrough TODO**, plus TODOs for `/tf`, `/reset_odom`, unstamped Twist, cutter/charge modules.

## Tests — all 24 pass here
- `test_protocol.py` (11): framing round-trips, escaping, bad-checksum resync, struct sizes, WIT scaling, and **bit-exact sub-packet histogram parity with the reference decoder on the 2.8 MB live capture**.
- `test_node_smoke.py` (12): battery/IMU/odom publishing, scale+clamp+timeout, heartbeat shape, both mower_sensor_info paths.
- `test_loopback.py` (1): real socat pty ↔ fake MCU ↔ node round trip (58 frames, 28 heartbeats, measured speed = commanded).

Tests use `ros_stubs.py` **only when ROS is absent**, so the same files run under `colcon test` in the container; `scripts/loopback_test.sh` is the interactive `ros2 run` version.
